  "description": "issue #679 (SP7): spec/turtles-and-sprites.md:108 — `xcor`, `ycor`, `heading`, and `pos` READ FROM THE CURRENT TURTLE, a whole spec bullet with no fixture before this slice. After `tell :a` plus `forward 30`/`right 90`, the four reporters see :a's own state (0, 30, 90, [0 30]); re-addressing the main turtle with `tell first turtles` makes those same four reporters report the untouched main turtle (0, 0, 0, [0 0]). Locks that the reporters follow the addressed set instead of reading one global turtle. Every change of the addressed set — here from `tell` — also emits the addressing `primitive` event carrying `addressing: { addressed_turtle_ids, current_turtle_id }`, so a consumer can identify the addressed turtle set (issue #766, spec/rendering.md:193); `ask`/`each` emit one again when the previous set is restored, on every exit path.",
